1
00:00:24,466 --> 00:00:26,133
No more fake-girlfriend gigs.

2
00:00:26,533 --> 00:00:28,166
No more getting paid to
break couples up.

3
00:00:28,566 --> 00:00:31,500
And no more dangerous jobs of any kind.

4
00:00:32,266 --> 00:00:33,066
Understand?

5
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:34,900
Help me!

6
00:00:35,766 --> 00:00:36,666
What are you doing?!

7
00:00:39,666 --> 00:00:42,166
I think there's a whole scheme
behind all of this.

8
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:45,600
I'll get to the bottom of it
and make sure they all go to prison.

9
00:00:48,331 --> 00:00:51,430
Chat:(Find me a good private
investigator for tomorrow.)

10
00:01:27,666 --> 00:01:28,466
Nant...

11
00:01:30,966 --> 00:01:32,066
Don't cry anymore.

12
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:34,200
Are you okay?

13
00:01:35,700 --> 00:01:36,900
Does anything hurt?

14
00:03:39,104 --> 00:03:41,104
(We need to meet. It's urgent.
Have the lawsuit documents ready.)

15
00:04:12,184 --> 00:04:13,100
Stay still!

16
00:04:13,804 --> 00:04:15,000
I'm not going.

17
00:04:15,001 --> 00:04:17,001
I'm not going, Mom.

18
00:04:17,375 --> 00:04:18,080
Mom!

19
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:18,599
Nant.

20
00:04:21,166 --> 00:04:22,133
Are you okay?

21
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:23,666
You look so pale.

22
00:04:24,066 --> 00:04:25,466
Was I being too loud?

23
00:04:26,566 --> 00:04:27,366
Uh...

24
00:04:28,966 --> 00:04:29,685
No.

25
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,760
It's fine.

26
00:04:32,238 --> 00:04:35,200
I was just lost in
thought for a moment.

27
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:38,982
Okay, then
please sign these documents for me.

28
00:04:38,982 --> 00:04:41,133
Take your time,
just do as much as you can handle.

29
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:42,500
Okay.

30
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:05,300
Nant.

31
00:05:08,533 --> 00:05:09,333
Are you okay?

32
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,566
Boss Chat sent this for you.

33
00:05:21,366 --> 00:05:23,500
She specifically asked me
to look after you.

34
00:05:24,166 --> 00:05:25,933
She doesn't want you
to overwork yourself.

35
00:05:29,733 --> 00:05:30,533
Thank you.

36
00:05:31,666 --> 00:05:34,766
I'll get back to work, then.

37
00:05:35,333 --> 00:05:36,133
Okay.

38
00:05:45,733 --> 00:05:49,202
And don't take
any of these kinds of jobs again.

39
00:05:49,584 --> 00:05:52,344
No matter how much
money anyone offers you.

40
00:05:52,678 --> 00:05:54,238
And don't ghost me for too long.

41
00:05:55,385 --> 00:05:57,840
Keep texting me like you used to.

42
00:06:05,904 --> 00:06:09,426
(I've arrived at the office.)

43
00:06:29,518 --> 00:06:34,672
(This shirt is so comfortable.)

44
00:06:34,672 --> 00:06:36,672
(I even sprayed
your perfume on it, Chat.)

45
00:06:36,739 --> 00:06:40,268
(It feels like you're hugging me.)
(I miss you so much.)

46
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:11,237
I've been a lawyer for years,

47
00:07:11,237 --> 00:07:14,404
but this is the most despicable
case I've ever seen.

48
00:07:14,404 --> 00:07:15,800
There's a ton of shady stuff
behind the scenes.

49
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:18,533
What have you found out?

50
00:07:19,366 --> 00:07:21,354
The one who took money from that
old tycoon

51
00:07:21,688 --> 00:07:24,100
was Sinee, Nant's mother.

52
00:07:25,733 --> 00:07:26,533
Seriously.

53
00:07:27,333 --> 00:07:29,066
She hasn't changed a bit.
Still up to her old tricks.

54
00:07:32,300 --> 00:07:33,800
What about Nant's room being trashed?

55
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:38,240
Sinee found out that
Nant had a rich girlfriend.

56
00:07:39,339 --> 00:07:41,337
And that she'd helped pay off
her grandparents' land debt.

57
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:44,194
So she wanted to bleed Nant dry.

58
00:07:44,194 --> 00:07:46,054
But she knew Nant wouldn't let her.

59
00:07:46,675 --> 00:07:48,259
That's why she hired people
to trash her room.

60
00:07:49,262 --> 00:07:52,202
Forcing Nant out with nowhere
to stay

61
00:07:52,536 --> 00:07:54,396
and zero cash for repairs.

62
00:07:55,366 --> 00:07:58,366
In the end, Nant had no choice
but to take the job from Wasu.

63
00:08:00,533 --> 00:08:02,166
What a piece of shit.

64
00:08:07,466 --> 00:08:09,566
Do we have enough evidence
to put them all behind bars?

65
00:08:10,366 --> 00:08:11,006
Absolutely.

66
00:08:11,484 --> 00:08:12,766
They'll be going to prison for sure.

67
00:08:13,166 --> 00:08:15,740
I'm definitely putting Wasu behind bars.

68
00:08:16,648 --> 00:08:17,751
But as for Nant's mother,

69
00:08:18,659 --> 00:08:20,500
I'd rather deal with her quietly.

70
00:08:23,766 --> 00:08:25,200
Are you just going
to let her get away with it?

71
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:28,766
Even with all
this evidence against her?

72
00:08:30,166 --> 00:08:30,966
Sigh...

73
00:08:31,966 --> 00:08:32,766
I'm not letting her off the hook.

74
00:08:34,066 --> 00:08:35,766
I just don't want Nant to find out

75
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:38,466
that her own mother sold her off again.

76
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:43,400
I don't want Nant to be hurt
by that woman all over again.

77
00:08:48,166 --> 00:08:48,966
Okay.

78
00:08:50,533 --> 00:08:52,533
I'll draft the contract for you, then.

79
00:08:54,566 --> 00:08:55,566
Thanks, girl.

80
00:08:56,500 --> 00:08:57,300
No problem.

81
00:08:58,300 --> 00:08:59,100
I'm off.

82
00:08:59,766 --> 00:09:01,200
Come on, I'll walk you out.

83
00:09:19,618 --> 00:09:21,533
Hello, Chom. What's up, sweetheart?

84
00:09:21,533 --> 00:09:22,533
Hello, Mom.

85
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:24,400
Mmm.

86
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:27,400
I don't know what's gotten into Chat.

87
00:09:27,933 --> 00:09:30,666
She's never been distracted
during a board meeting before.

88
00:09:30,865 --> 00:09:32,700
Really?

89
00:09:32,700 --> 00:09:33,988
Yes, Mom. I have no idea
what's going on either.

90
00:09:34,466 --> 00:09:36,360
I have no idea
what's going on either.

91
00:09:36,360 --> 00:09:39,266
Don't worry, I'll subtly question
Jaokha maybe we might get something.

92
00:09:39,266 --> 00:09:43,387
Could this have something
to do with that intern named Nant?

93
00:09:44,166 --> 00:09:45,600
I think so too, Mom.

94
00:09:46,366 --> 00:09:49,000
It must have something to do with Nant.

95
00:09:55,333 --> 00:09:56,133
Okay.

96
00:09:56,933 --> 00:09:57,800
Just a moment, Mom.

97
00:09:58,600 --> 00:09:59,400
Well, well...

98
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:01,966
Were you talking about Mr. Chat?

99
00:10:03,733 --> 00:10:06,166
Yes. Is there something you need,
Ms. Sopha?

100
00:10:07,166 --> 00:10:08,542
It's nothing, really.

101
00:10:09,068 --> 00:10:10,755
I just wanted to
ask you

102
00:10:10,755 --> 00:10:12,864
to remind Ms. Chat.

103
00:10:13,103 --> 00:10:16,605
That this afternoon's board
meeting is very important.

104
00:10:18,266 --> 00:10:19,440
What do you mean by that? Hmm?

105
00:10:20,700 --> 00:10:24,364
If our CEO keeps getting distracted

106
00:10:25,129 --> 00:10:26,478
instead of focusing on work,

107
00:10:27,290 --> 00:10:29,133
and worrying about personal matters

108
00:10:29,659 --> 00:10:31,197
I'm afraid.
Mr. Chat's image.

109
00:10:32,105 --> 00:10:35,920
It could hurt
Mr. Chat's image.

110
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:52,400
Huh?

111
00:10:53,881 --> 00:10:54,613
Only a hundred thousand?

112
00:10:55,712 --> 00:10:59,856
Are you sure this is
what my daughter is worth, counselor?

113
00:10:59,856 --> 00:11:01,300
Why is it so little?

114
00:11:02,066 --> 00:11:04,866
You say 'what your daughter
is worth' so shamelessly.

115
00:11:05,566 --> 00:11:06,367
What?

116
00:11:06,988 --> 00:11:09,866
should I call
it a mother's milk fee?

117
00:11:11,800 --> 00:11:13,400
You really have no shame, do you?

118
00:11:14,066 --> 00:11:14,623
Why ?

119
00:11:15,101 --> 00:11:16,473
Why should I care?

120
00:11:16,999 --> 00:11:18,540
I'm her mother.

121
00:11:18,922 --> 00:11:20,865
I can do whatever
I want with my own daughter.

122
00:11:20,865 --> 00:11:22,882
Is there any law that says I can't?

123
00:11:24,333 --> 00:11:26,482
The law doesn't forbid
a mother from loving her child.

124
00:11:26,769 --> 00:11:29,932
But there's a specific section of the
law that addresses human trafficking.

125
00:11:29,932 --> 00:11:32,420
Would you like me to recite
it for you, ma'am?

126
00:11:33,100 --> 00:11:34,766
Go ahead.
I won't remember any of it anyway.

127
00:11:37,900 --> 00:11:40,850
Counselor, have a little sympathy for
me.

128
00:11:41,232 --> 00:11:43,166
Raising Nant wasn't easy, you know.

129
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:45,533
When exactly was it difficult for you?

130
00:11:46,533 --> 00:11:48,853
Was it when you sent her
to live with her grandparents,

131
00:11:48,853 --> 00:11:51,700
or now, when you're sitting here
negotiating her price?

132
00:11:52,533 --> 00:11:54,559
Hey, don't just make stuff up!

133
00:11:55,228 --> 00:11:57,679
I carried her and suffered through
childbirth for her.

134
00:11:57,679 --> 00:11:59,700
She owes me her whole life!

135
00:12:01,066 --> 00:12:02,866
I don't make things up, ma'am.

136
00:12:04,333 --> 00:12:05,966
Especially not the information
in this file.

137
00:12:09,566 --> 00:12:11,600
The main suspect Wasu
has confessed everything.

138
00:12:11,733 --> 00:12:12,666
He's told us everything,

139
00:12:13,866 --> 00:12:16,466
including the names of everyone
who took his money.

140
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:20,600
Let him say whatever he wants.
Do you have any proof?

141
00:12:20,966 --> 00:12:22,145
Of course I do.

142
00:12:22,145 --> 00:12:23,599
Bank transfer slips,

143
00:12:23,599 --> 00:12:24,997
audio recordings on the phone,

144
00:12:24,997 --> 00:12:27,650
chat records, CCTV footage.

145
00:12:29,179 --> 00:12:30,934
I have it all.

146
00:12:32,766 --> 00:12:34,400
Human trafficking.

147
00:12:35,021 --> 00:12:37,258
Procuring women for exploitation,

148
00:12:37,592 --> 00:12:39,521
fraud, and money laundering.

149
00:12:39,521 --> 00:12:42,527
Honestly, that first charge alone

150
00:12:42,527 --> 00:12:44,166
will have you dying in prison.

151
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:45,200
Half a million.

152
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:46,766
I'll sign it right now.

153
00:12:47,066 --> 00:12:47,766
No.

154
00:12:47,766 --> 00:12:48,566
One million.

155
00:12:48,666 --> 00:12:50,700
Doesn't Nant have a rich girlfriend?

156
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:53,466
She can surely afford that much.

157
00:12:55,533 --> 00:12:57,100
May I say something?

158
00:12:58,100 --> 00:12:59,900
I've dealt with a lot of
terrible people myself.

159
00:13:01,166 --> 00:13:06,100
But you're easily one of the top five
most despicable people I've ever met.

160
00:13:06,533 --> 00:13:08,566
If you don't increase
the amount, Counselor,

161
00:13:09,166 --> 00:13:12,200
I'll expose all of this online.

162
00:13:13,066 --> 00:13:15,207
That a famous CEO

163
00:13:15,876 --> 00:13:19,305
is dating
a girl sold by her own mother.

164
00:13:47,666 --> 00:13:48,466
Hello.

165
00:13:49,900 --> 00:13:50,700
Is this the landlord?

166
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:53,000
Um, about the room payment...

167
00:13:55,466 --> 00:13:56,266
Huh?

168
00:13:57,600 --> 00:13:58,566
It's already paid?

169
00:14:01,966 --> 00:14:03,366
And the repairs are almost done too?

170
00:14:08,966 --> 00:14:09,766
Okay.

171
00:14:10,366 --> 00:14:11,100
Thank you.

172
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:11,900
Thank you so much.

173
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:19,166
This must be Chat's doing.

174
00:14:23,133 --> 00:14:24,133
I feel so lonely.

175
00:14:25,166 --> 00:14:27,566
I wonder if you're coming back
to the apartment yet.

176
00:14:30,066 --> 00:14:30,900
Never mind.

177
00:15:04,200 --> 00:15:05,277
It's all settled.

178
00:15:05,659 --> 00:15:08,382
Sinee agreed to sign
the contract and took the money.

179
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:16,066
Was it really that easy
to get her to agree?

180
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:18,373
Easy?

181
00:15:18,899 --> 00:15:20,649
She demanded another million.

182
00:15:20,936 --> 00:15:22,184
And even threatened to

183
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:23,784
expose everything on social media.

184
00:15:27,300 --> 00:15:29,210
Shameless people really

185
00:15:29,736 --> 00:15:31,700
never change, do they?

186
00:15:32,275 --> 00:15:32,966
Yeah.

187
00:15:34,113 --> 00:15:35,810
If she doesn't stop meddling,

188
00:15:36,192 --> 00:15:39,782
I'll send the case to the prosecutor
and put her away for good.

189
00:15:41,300 --> 00:15:42,600
Thanks, Jaokha.

190
00:15:43,800 --> 00:15:45,600
It's my job as a lawyer.

191
00:15:45,933 --> 00:15:46,766
There's something else.

192
00:15:47,533 --> 00:15:48,333
I saw it, you know.

193
00:15:48,500 --> 00:15:51,300
I was itching to get my hands on her.

194
00:15:57,333 --> 00:16:00,100
Jaokha, you know what?

195
00:16:01,533 --> 00:16:03,266
The moment I saw that photo

196
00:16:03,900 --> 00:16:04,900
at the hotel,

197
00:16:06,266 --> 00:16:07,300
I nearly lost my mind.

198
00:16:08,500 --> 00:16:09,900
Just hearing your voice,

199
00:16:10,500 --> 00:16:11,300
I knew right away

200
00:16:11,366 --> 00:16:12,866
someone was going to die tomorrow.

201
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:15,600
I don't care if it's her mother

202
00:16:16,533 --> 00:16:18,066
or whoever the hell it is.

203
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:20,966
If anyone even thinks
about laying a hand on Nant,

204
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:24,400
I won't let them get away with it.

205
00:16:26,266 --> 00:16:27,066
Yeah.

206
00:16:27,966 --> 00:16:28,800
Whatever happens, just tell me.

207
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:30,566
I'll always be here to help.

208
00:16:31,700 --> 00:16:32,700
Thanks, girl.

209
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:36,730
I'm heading out.

210
00:16:37,590 --> 00:16:39,117
Nant's waiting at the condo.

211
00:16:39,499 --> 00:16:41,182
and must be boring by now.

212
00:16:41,933 --> 00:16:45,133
Yeah, go ahead.
I'll take care of the rest.

213
00:16:45,629 --> 00:16:47,629
Thank you.

214
00:17:16,871 --> 00:17:17,496
Here.

215
00:17:25,800 --> 00:17:26,700
What's all this?

216
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:29,566
You suddenly show up
with flowers and snacks.

217
00:17:31,066 --> 00:17:31,866
Uh...

218
00:17:32,866 --> 00:17:34,900
I just found the flowers
near the office.

219
00:17:35,366 --> 00:17:38,666
And someone gave me the snacks.

220
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:43,400
Oh, really?

221
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:47,066
Just kidding.

222
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:48,300
That's not true.

223
00:17:48,933 --> 00:17:50,100
I bought them myself.

224
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:53,800
Did you buy these for me?

225
00:17:54,800 --> 00:17:55,600
Mm-hmm.

226
00:17:56,166 --> 00:17:56,966
They're for you.

227
00:17:59,333 --> 00:18:00,133
Is it heavy?

228
00:18:00,300 --> 00:18:01,666
We can put them down together.

229
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,300
There's so much
of your favorite stuff here.

230
00:18:16,100 --> 00:18:17,300
You bought all this for me?

231
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:18,800
Mm-hmm.

232
00:18:19,166 --> 00:18:19,966
It's for you.

233
00:18:21,533 --> 00:18:23,200
But why did you buy all this for me?

234
00:18:25,600 --> 00:18:26,466
Because...

235
00:18:28,766 --> 00:18:29,933
I missed you.

236
00:18:31,366 --> 00:18:33,566
Oh, I missed you, too.

237
00:18:37,333 --> 00:18:39,066
We work in the same building,

238
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:40,766
but we never get to see each other.

239
00:18:41,966 --> 00:18:43,266
I was practically dying without you.

240
00:18:47,933 --> 00:18:49,366
Aww, aww, aww...

241
00:18:51,333 --> 00:18:52,166
Really?

242
00:18:53,366 --> 00:18:54,166
I mean it.

243
00:18:56,133 --> 00:18:58,066
And after I've been so good to you...

244
00:19:00,166 --> 00:19:02,200
How do you think you should reward me?

245
00:19:12,266 --> 00:19:15,166
When you texted saying
the AC in your room was freezing...

246
00:19:16,266 --> 00:19:17,100
Were you freezing?

247
00:19:20,333 --> 00:19:21,300
Very much so.

248
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:23,300
Really?

249
00:19:24,600 --> 00:19:25,400
Yes.

250
00:19:27,100 --> 00:19:28,800
Then let's take a warm shower together.

251
00:19:31,533 --> 00:19:33,700
Who said I'd shower with you?

252
00:19:35,066 --> 00:19:36,333
Go shower by yourself.

253
00:19:38,266 --> 00:19:39,066
Hey!

254
00:19:39,866 --> 00:19:40,666
Why not?

255
00:19:41,933 --> 00:19:43,866
Because I want to shower with you.

256
00:19:46,533 --> 00:19:48,000
Come on, let's shower together.

257
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:50,300
Let's take a shower together.

258
00:19:51,091 --> 00:19:51,591
No.

259
00:19:51,825 --> 00:19:53,825
Please.

260
00:19:55,201 --> 00:19:56,054
Come on,

261
00:19:56,441 --> 00:19:57,581
Nant. Hurry up.

262
00:19:58,607 --> 00:20:00,607
Come on,

263
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:01,800
Go.

264
00:20:02,066 --> 00:20:02,671
No.

265
00:20:02,671 --> 00:20:03,700
Let's shower together.

266
00:20:04,733 --> 00:20:05,533
Nant.

267
00:20:06,366 --> 00:20:07,400
If you don't go,

268
00:20:08,766 --> 00:20:10,000
I'll carry you there myself.

269
00:20:11,166 --> 00:20:13,166
Okay, okay, okay!

270
00:20:14,897 --> 00:20:16,611
Ice: (Can you come to my room?)

271
00:20:16,611 --> 00:20:18,264
Kirin: (Why do I have to?)

272
00:20:31,300 --> 00:20:32,166
Come in first.

273
00:20:42,066 --> 00:20:42,866
Have a seat.

274
00:20:57,400 --> 00:20:59,000
You called me over
in the middle of the night.

275
00:21:00,500 --> 00:21:01,300
What's going on?

276
00:21:04,066 --> 00:21:06,600
I just bought some new lipstick,

277
00:21:07,066 --> 00:21:09,266
so I wanted you to help me try it out

278
00:21:10,333 --> 00:21:11,666
and see which shade suits me best.

279
00:21:15,100 --> 00:21:15,900
That's it?

280
00:21:17,500 --> 00:21:18,300
Yeah.

281
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:19,600
That's all.

282
00:21:20,700 --> 00:21:21,500
Take a look.

283
00:21:38,566 --> 00:21:41,300
What do you think?
Does this shade look good?

284
00:21:46,366 --> 00:21:47,300
It's pretty.

285
00:21:48,266 --> 00:21:49,966
It's a little bold, though.

286
00:21:50,898 --> 00:21:52,898
Still, it suits you.

287
00:21:54,310 --> 00:21:56,310
I don't think

288
00:21:56,500 --> 00:21:58,200
it really suits me.

289
00:21:59,700 --> 00:22:00,933
Then who does it suit?

290
00:22:03,300 --> 00:22:04,466
It suits you, actually.

291
00:22:25,566 --> 00:22:26,366
What's that for?

292
00:22:27,533 --> 00:22:29,133
Why did you suddenly kiss me?

293
00:22:29,561 --> 00:22:30,960
You startle me!

294
00:22:31,592 --> 00:22:33,592
I just wanted to test it out to see...

295
00:22:34,366 --> 00:22:36,200
Did the lipstick
come off when we kissed?

296
00:22:38,600 --> 00:22:41,100
But I don't think
that was enough, was it?

297
00:22:43,666 --> 00:22:44,766
What do you mean?

298
00:22:45,933 --> 00:22:47,733
We usually use our tongues, don't we?

299
00:23:18,933 --> 00:23:20,166
What are you planning to do?

300
00:23:22,800 --> 00:23:24,000
I just want to find out

301
00:23:25,566 --> 00:23:27,066
how many kisses it'll take

302
00:23:28,166 --> 00:23:30,400
to wipe all the lipstick off my lips.

303
00:23:53,333 --> 00:23:54,666
Do you have any plans tomorrow?

304
00:23:56,366 --> 00:23:57,166
No, I don't.

305
00:23:58,300 --> 00:23:59,100
Why?

306
00:24:01,566 --> 00:24:05,066
Then stay with me all night tonight.

307
00:24:58,300 --> 00:24:59,400
Are you still cold?

308
00:25:05,200 --> 00:25:06,000
Yes.

309
00:26:53,566 --> 00:26:55,500
We can't. We'll be late.

310
00:26:57,500 --> 00:27:00,900
Whoa, you're nagging just like Chom.

311
00:27:05,066 --> 00:27:06,933
By the way, this shirt
is a little too tight.

312
00:27:07,533 --> 00:27:08,866
Go change into something else.

313
00:27:09,700 --> 00:27:10,500
I'm jealous.

314
00:27:13,100 --> 00:27:13,900
Jealous?

315
00:27:14,400 --> 00:27:16,600
Or are you afraid you won't be
able to control yourself at work?

316
00:27:25,665 --> 00:27:28,600
Oh, I was actually planning
to go back to my room today.

317
00:27:30,400 --> 00:27:32,771
I've already paid for
the repairs to your room.

318
00:27:33,153 --> 00:27:34,729
It should be finished today.

319
00:27:35,494 --> 00:27:36,799
But...

320
00:27:37,516 --> 00:27:39,422
I don't think you'll be able
to move back in just yet.

321
00:27:40,569 --> 00:27:41,585
There's still dust

322
00:27:41,824 --> 00:27:42,709
and paint fumes everywhere.

323
00:27:44,800 --> 00:27:46,166
You'd get sick if you stayed there.

324
00:27:46,533 --> 00:27:48,733
And if you got sick
and couldn't come to work...

325
00:27:49,166 --> 00:27:49,966
Well...

326
00:27:50,700 --> 00:27:51,766
You'd be in big trouble.

327
00:27:52,800 --> 00:27:53,666
How about this?

328
00:27:54,566 --> 00:27:56,766
Why don't you just stay here?

329
00:27:57,500 --> 00:27:58,300
Hmm?

330
00:27:59,000 --> 00:27:59,800
What do you say?

331
00:28:01,666 --> 00:28:02,466
Oh...

332
00:28:03,666 --> 00:28:05,866
I don't want to impose on you, Chat.

333
00:28:09,900 --> 00:28:12,733
If you say you're imposing
on me even once,

334
00:28:13,733 --> 00:28:16,300
I'll make sure you won't
be able to leave this room.

335
00:28:20,800 --> 00:28:22,733
You want to stay with me?

336
00:28:24,966 --> 00:28:26,566
You've already lost to me, haven't you?

337
00:28:31,733 --> 00:28:32,533
Oh.

338
00:28:34,933 --> 00:28:36,766
We're really going to be late for work.

339
00:28:39,300 --> 00:28:40,933
So protective of yourself, huh?

340
00:28:44,600 --> 00:28:46,466
I'm done. Go to work already.

341
00:28:47,500 --> 00:28:48,300
Okay, okay.

342
00:29:02,500 --> 00:29:03,300
Wear it right.

343
00:29:05,600 --> 00:29:07,266
Okay, okay, go ahead then.

344
00:29:41,400 --> 00:29:44,192
Hey, you need to go to work now

345
00:29:44,192 --> 00:29:47,100
your patients must be waiting on you.

346
00:29:47,766 --> 00:29:52,014
Can I stay in bed a little longer?
You were too rough with me last night.

347
00:29:52,014 --> 00:29:52,700
I'm exhausted.

348
00:29:53,533 --> 00:29:57,600
What do you mean rough? Up, now!
Do you even know what time it is?

349
00:30:03,900 --> 00:30:05,500
I'm the owner of the hospital.

350
00:30:06,500 --> 00:30:07,966
I can go to work or not.
It's up to me.

351
00:30:09,066 --> 00:30:09,866
Huh?

352
00:30:10,466 --> 00:30:11,333
The hospital owner?

353
00:30:15,533 --> 00:30:17,900
What's so surprising?
I'm just the hospital owner.

354
00:30:24,366 --> 00:30:26,366
I've already given myself the day off.

355
00:30:27,700 --> 00:30:29,066
And don't you dare go anywhere.

356
00:30:29,700 --> 00:30:30,500
Understand?

357
00:30:34,300 --> 00:30:35,100
Get some sleep.

358
00:30:47,100 --> 00:30:51,533
Then, can we go for another round?

359
00:30:53,933 --> 00:30:55,500
If you're not tired, sure.

360
00:31:06,700 --> 00:31:07,766
Take it easy, will you?

361
00:31:31,066 --> 00:31:34,926
Secretary Han, Do you know why Boss
is so devoted to her work?

362
00:31:34,926 --> 00:31:36,408
What CEO goes to

363
00:31:36,838 --> 00:31:38,333
the office every single day?

364
00:31:40,300 --> 00:31:41,100
Umm...

365
00:31:43,933 --> 00:31:46,800
Boss probably loves
her partner more than his work.

366
00:31:47,600 --> 00:31:48,400
Oops!

367
00:31:49,266 --> 00:31:51,600
Wait, is Boss seeing someone?

368
00:31:55,300 --> 00:31:57,566
I can't even imagine what Boss
would be like in a relationship.

369
00:31:59,500 --> 00:32:03,500
Probably a ruthless CEO
all slapping and kissing, right?

370
00:32:03,733 --> 00:32:05,850
No, I don't think so.

371
00:32:05,850 --> 00:32:09,019
The boss seems like the type
who likes to peck.

372
00:32:09,497 --> 00:32:12,900
She's like a chicken. You know how
chickens peck? They just won't let go.

373
00:32:13,200 --> 00:32:14,918
Just picturing it makes me wanna cry

374
00:32:14,918 --> 00:32:17,330
she's that's pure ice-cold.

375
00:32:22,533 --> 00:32:26,166
I think you guys are reading way
too much into it.

376
00:32:28,600 --> 00:32:29,726
I think

377
00:32:30,491 --> 00:32:34,891
Boss Chat would be would
be really sweet in a relationship.

378
00:32:39,430 --> 00:32:40,540
Really sweet...

379
00:32:40,866 --> 00:32:42,022
So sweet...

380
00:32:42,022 --> 00:32:43,476
it's actually terrifying.

381
00:32:46,009 --> 00:32:47,089
Boss.

382
00:32:49,200 --> 00:32:50,000
What's so terrifying?

383
00:32:51,066 --> 00:32:53,100
You mean your little brother, right?

384
00:32:53,466 --> 00:32:54,266
Huh?

385
00:32:56,733 --> 00:33:00,200
Thitinant, come to my office right now.

386
00:33:01,966 --> 00:33:02,766
Yes.

387
00:33:06,800 --> 00:33:09,166
Oh, um... I'll leave
my bag here for now.

388
00:33:09,733 --> 00:33:10,533
Sure, sure.

389
00:33:36,066 --> 00:33:37,966
What were they gossiping
about me this time?

390
00:33:38,933 --> 00:33:39,733
Oh, no.

391
00:33:40,366 --> 00:33:41,900
It wasn't exactly gossip.

392
00:33:42,533 --> 00:33:43,966
We were just making guesses.

393
00:33:45,266 --> 00:33:46,100
Just guesses?

394
00:33:47,400 --> 00:33:48,200
Guessing about what?

395
00:33:48,566 --> 00:33:49,366
Oh.

396
00:33:50,300 --> 00:33:51,533
If I were you, Boss,

397
00:33:52,133 --> 00:33:53,400
I wouldn't want to know.

398
00:33:55,666 --> 00:33:56,466
If you say it like that.

399
00:33:57,666 --> 00:33:59,300
Now you've made me curious.

400
00:34:00,866 --> 00:34:01,666
Sigh...

401
00:34:01,666 --> 00:34:05,300
Anyway, was there something
you wanted to see me about, Boss?

402
00:34:10,366 --> 00:34:11,766
About his document,

403
00:34:12,500 --> 00:34:13,366
Who prepared it?

404
00:34:14,500 --> 00:34:15,300
I did.

405
00:34:15,733 --> 00:34:18,666
Why? Is something wrong?
What's the matter?

406
00:34:24,966 --> 00:34:26,527
I'm pretty good, aren't I?

407
00:34:27,196 --> 00:34:28,469
I even guessed correctly

408
00:34:29,090 --> 00:34:30,700
that this document was yours.

409
00:34:32,533 --> 00:34:33,033
So...

410
00:34:33,320 --> 00:34:35,087
What's wrong with it?

411
00:34:37,466 --> 00:34:38,866
Nothing's wrong with it.

412
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:41,437
I called you in to compliment you.

413
00:34:42,632 --> 00:34:43,514
You're so good.

414
00:34:44,231 --> 00:34:45,409
You deserve a reward.

415
00:34:47,500 --> 00:34:48,882
No, Boss.

416
00:34:49,647 --> 00:34:51,491
Someone might see us.

417
00:34:53,259 --> 00:34:54,744
We're in the office, you know.

418
00:34:57,300 --> 00:35:01,400
Who would dare walk into
my office without knocking?

419
00:35:13,466 --> 00:35:15,000
See? I told you.

420
00:35:18,338 --> 00:35:21,700
What about Nant, Boss?

421
00:35:22,700 --> 00:35:23,500
She's already left.

422
00:35:24,366 --> 00:35:25,166
Oh, really?

423
00:35:25,766 --> 00:35:26,533
Yeah.

424
00:35:26,533 --> 00:35:27,942
I just saw her

425
00:35:28,276 --> 00:35:30,285
follow you into
your office a moment ago, though.

426
00:35:35,266 --> 00:35:36,466
Uh, Hanna.

427
00:35:36,933 --> 00:35:37,733
Uh...

428
00:35:38,066 --> 00:35:38,733
Yes?

429
00:35:38,733 --> 00:35:39,566
Did you need something?

430
00:35:40,933 --> 00:35:41,666
Oh...

431
00:35:41,666 --> 00:35:45,166
I was just coming to ask about
your schedule for next month, Boss.

432
00:35:47,300 --> 00:35:48,100
Yes, Boss.

433
00:35:48,566 --> 00:35:49,366
Stop.

434
00:35:50,733 --> 00:35:51,533
Yes?

435
00:35:53,200 --> 00:35:54,722
I mean,

436
00:35:55,391 --> 00:35:58,181
I'd like to take a day off for
a health checkup next month.

437
00:35:58,611 --> 00:36:01,800
You can make the appointment
and put it on my schedule.

438
00:36:02,766 --> 00:36:03,750
Of course, Boss.

439
00:36:05,566 --> 00:36:06,449
But...

440
00:36:07,666 --> 00:36:08,966
Are you okay, Boss?

441
00:36:10,200 --> 00:36:12,566
Why does your face look so red?

442
00:36:14,166 --> 00:36:16,333
Would you like me
to get you some medicine?

443
00:36:16,866 --> 00:36:17,666
I'm fine.

444
00:36:19,766 --> 00:36:20,990
Really, Boss?

445
00:36:22,089 --> 00:36:24,676
You don't look very well.

446
00:36:24,676 --> 00:36:26,727
Or maybe you...

447
00:36:27,539 --> 00:36:28,945
Umm...Boss.

448
00:36:28,945 --> 00:36:29,566
Ouch!

449
00:36:30,333 --> 00:36:32,966
Put it down and leave.

450
00:36:33,666 --> 00:36:36,078
Okay, I'll leave it right here, then.

451
00:36:36,795 --> 00:36:39,863
Put it down and leave.
Okay, I'll leave it right here, then.

452
00:36:40,675 --> 00:36:41,533
Get out.

453
00:36:43,158 --> 00:36:44,073
Okay.

454
00:36:58,700 --> 00:37:00,000
You can come out now, Nant.

455
00:37:16,366 --> 00:37:18,966
Your face just now was so funny.

456
00:37:22,000 --> 00:37:23,800
Never thought you had t
his playful side.

457
00:37:25,000 --> 00:37:25,900
You little brat.

458
00:37:26,666 --> 00:37:28,266
Weren't you worried
someone might see us?

459
00:37:28,900 --> 00:37:31,000
Well, Boss started it.

460
00:37:53,533 --> 00:37:54,333
Wait a minute.

461
00:37:58,466 --> 00:37:59,333
You can't touch there.

462
00:38:26,000 --> 00:38:27,891
We were just going to
watch a movie at home.

463
00:38:27,891 --> 00:38:29,899
Why did you buy so much stuff?

464
00:38:29,899 --> 00:38:32,200
It's like you're preparing
to open a convenience store.

465
00:38:34,400 --> 00:38:36,133
You're right. I'm sorry.

466
00:38:37,133 --> 00:38:39,266
Hey, what are you apologizing for?

467
00:38:40,333 --> 00:38:42,482
It's fine. You're with me now.

468
00:38:42,482 --> 00:38:45,557
Buy whatever you want and
eat whatever you like.

469
00:38:45,987 --> 00:38:48,270
You can even use my card.
There's no limit.

470
00:38:50,766 --> 00:38:52,933
Why are you so nice to me, Chat?

471
00:38:55,600 --> 00:38:59,133
Because you're good at your job.
I have to reward you.

472
00:39:03,733 --> 00:39:07,200
Great at my job,
or great at something else?

473
00:39:10,500 --> 00:39:14,166
Well, I'm not sure.

474
00:39:19,933 --> 00:39:23,566
So that means I'm not
good at anything else?

475
00:39:26,533 --> 00:39:30,300
Just kidding.
You're good at everything.

476
00:39:33,500 --> 00:39:34,300
Really?

477
00:39:34,800 --> 00:39:35,600
Yeah.

478
00:39:39,500 --> 00:39:40,300
And this...

479
00:39:41,666 --> 00:39:44,100
Is this the special dinner
you told me about?

480
00:39:46,266 --> 00:39:47,066
Yes.

481
00:39:47,733 --> 00:39:48,766
Surprised?

482
00:39:49,533 --> 00:39:50,333
Uh...

483
00:39:51,100 --> 00:39:51,900
Yeah.

484
00:39:59,466 --> 00:40:01,600
Have you ever done this for
anyone before, Chat?

485
00:40:03,533 --> 00:40:04,619
Never.

486
00:40:05,049 --> 00:40:07,061
My life is usually
much quieter than this.

487
00:40:08,866 --> 00:40:11,566
Is having me around a good thing?

488
00:40:15,533 --> 00:40:16,666
It's better than I expected.

489
00:40:21,000 --> 00:40:22,166
But it's better without anyone.

490
00:40:22,900 --> 00:40:24,266
Because I like keeping things quiet.

491
00:40:29,466 --> 00:40:30,386
How boring.

492
00:41:00,300 --> 00:41:01,293
Ooh, hot!

493
00:41:01,293 --> 00:41:01,800
Hey!

494
00:41:02,966 --> 00:41:03,800
Let me see.

495
00:41:04,400 --> 00:41:05,500
Did you burn your tongue?

496
00:41:11,600 --> 00:41:13,933
I thought you said having someone
around wasn't a good thing.

497
00:41:19,300 --> 00:41:20,466
Are you sulking?

498
00:41:21,466 --> 00:41:23,366
Do you even have the right
to sulk with me?

499
00:41:24,166 --> 00:41:24,966
Hmm?

500
00:41:27,166 --> 00:41:28,166
Hurry up and eat.

501
00:41:29,066 --> 00:41:30,200
We're out of the other noodles.

502
00:41:35,300 --> 00:41:37,133
I don't want noodles anymore.

503
00:41:49,733 --> 00:41:50,966
Then what do you want?

504
00:42:26,159 --> 00:42:29,206
Okay, okay! Your stomach's growling
so loudly.

505
00:42:29,779 --> 00:42:31,373
Just eat your fill first.

506
00:42:33,866 --> 00:42:35,300
So embarrassing.

507
00:42:40,333 --> 00:42:41,466
I'll feed you.

508
00:42:47,500 --> 00:42:48,200
Here.

509
00:42:48,200 --> 00:42:49,000
Ahm.

510
00:43:08,533 --> 00:43:09,400
This is delicious.

511
00:43:11,166 --> 00:43:12,500
You've got magic hands.

512
00:43:33,266 --> 00:43:34,466
Are you done eating?

513
00:43:46,466 --> 00:43:47,966
Once you're done, go take a shower.

514
00:43:48,966 --> 00:43:50,733
I bought you some pajamas, too.

515
00:44:16,500 --> 00:44:17,600
Chat, do you think...

516
00:44:20,200 --> 00:44:21,566
Is this too revealing?

517
00:44:22,566 --> 00:44:23,366
Not at all.

518
00:44:24,466 --> 00:44:26,300
You look even better
in it than I imagined.

519
00:44:27,866 --> 00:44:28,666
Come here.

520
00:44:48,533 --> 00:44:50,166
Chat, the way you're staring at me...

521
00:44:51,166 --> 00:44:52,566
I can get shy too, you know.

522
00:44:58,466 --> 00:45:00,933
You were staring at me
just fine this afternoon.

523
00:45:02,700 --> 00:45:04,366
Now it's my turn to look at you.

524
00:45:54,333 --> 00:45:55,900
You've looked at me enough already.

525
00:46:10,466 --> 00:46:11,600
You don't have to look anymore.

526
00:46:15,933 --> 00:46:17,566
Just feel that I'm here.

527
00:46:26,328 --> 00:46:28,328
That I'm the one

528
00:46:31,800 --> 00:46:32,600
who's going to tie you up.

529
00:47:24,400 --> 00:47:27,000
Chat, can you stay by my side
like this forever?

530
00:47:30,566 --> 00:47:31,366
Of course.

531
00:47:33,700 --> 00:47:34,866
Forever.

532
00:48:38,698 --> 00:48:43,899
(I have an off-site meeting today.
See you tonight at the condo.)

533
00:48:56,766 --> 00:48:57,566
Nant.

534
00:48:59,333 --> 00:49:00,933
Ms. Chawi would like to see you.

535
00:49:01,866 --> 00:49:03,933
She's waiting at the café downstairs.

536
00:49:13,000 --> 00:49:13,800
Okay.

537
00:49:15,966 --> 00:49:16,866
It's okay.

538
00:49:47,133 --> 00:49:48,333
What's going on?

539
00:50:02,363 --> 00:50:04,898
(Ms. Chat, Ms. Chawi
wants to see Nant.)

540
00:50:22,933 --> 00:50:25,666
Did you investigate my background?

541
00:50:26,166 --> 00:50:27,716
I want to meet the person

542
00:50:27,716 --> 00:50:30,700
my daughter keeps having
over to stay at her condo.

543
00:50:31,066 --> 00:50:34,366
I feel like we're just
so different from each other.

544
00:50:35,000 --> 00:50:37,529
Please tell me what
my mother said to you

545
00:50:37,920 --> 00:50:39,733
that make you overthink
and feel so down.

546
